5. Current Project Status
The project has successfully completed the machine learning pipeline, Flask backend development, frontend integration, prediction history logging, and Apache Spark analytics. Users can enter soil and environmental parameters through the web interface and receive real-time crop recommendations generated by the trained Gaussian Naive Bayes model.
Prediction history is automatically stored in a CSV file, and Apache Spark processes this data to generate analytical insights such as total predictions, most recommended crop, average temperature, average rainfall, and crop distribution.
Apache Hive integration is currently in progress and will be used to store and query prediction history using SQL-like operations as part of the Big Data component of the project.
6. Dataset Description
The Crop Recommendation Dataset is used to train the machine learning model. It contains information about soil nutrients and environmental conditions required for crop growth. The dataset consists of multiple instances representing different agricultural conditions and their corresponding recommended crops.
The input features used in this project are:
Feature	Description
Nitrogen (N)	Nitrogen content in the soil
Phosphorus (P)	Phosphorus content in the soil
Potassium (K)	Potassium content in the soil
Temperature	Average temperature (°C)
Humidity	Relative humidity (%)
pH	Soil pH value
Rainfall	Rainfall received (mm)


The target variable is the crop that is most suitable for cultivation under the given conditions.
Before training, the dataset was examined for missing values, duplicate records, and inconsistent data types. The feature names were standardized and the target labels were encoded into numerical values for machine learning.
